GARDEN CONDITIONAL USE LICENSE v0.2

This is a custom conditional-use license. It is not an OSI-approved open-source
license.

1. Scope

Subject to applicable law and only to the extent the relevant rights are legally
protectable and licensable, this license applies to the copyrightable material,
software, specifications, documentation, protected inventions, designs, and
implementations disclosed in this repository ("Covered Garden Material").

Nothing in this license creates an intellectual-property right that does not
otherwise exist under applicable law.

2. Permission for Garden use only

You may copy, modify, implement, run, distribute, and otherwise use Covered
Garden Material only as part of a Garden implementation that:

(a) is actually governed by the applicable ratified Garden rules rather than
merely using the Garden name;

(b) preserves the applicable Garden requirements for human sovereignty, rights,
privacy, consent, bounded authority, evidence/provenance, auditability, and
other mandatory constitutional or safety rules; and

(c) complies with the Garden economic contribution/tax rule in Section 3.

Permission under this license is conditional on continued compliance with these
requirements.

3. Garden economic contribution / tax rule

For a natural person's annual income or earnings, let M be the median individual
income in the person's applicable local economic geography, as determined under
the applicable Garden economic rules.

The required Garden income contribution/tax schedule is:

- income at or below 1 x M: 0%;
- income above 1 x M and below 20 x M: a progressive effective rate that rises
  from 0% toward 50%;
- income at or above 20 x M: 50%.

The intermediate schedule must be implemented so that after-contribution income
strictly increases as gross income increases; earning more must not reduce
after-contribution income. The more precise current ratified Garden economic
rule controls the intermediate curve, income definition, measurement period,
economic-geography definition, collection mechanism, exemptions, and audit
rules, provided it preserves the endpoints above unless a later valid Garden
constitutional process changes them.

The applicable local economic geography should be a stable labour/economic
market area rather than an arbitrary small administrative boundary, using the
current Garden methodology for population sufficiency and smoothed/rolling
income measurement.

For organizations, cooperatives, projects, or other entities, compliance is
determined under the applicable Garden economic and beneficial-ownership rules.
This license does not create a separate corporation-level tax where Garden rules
allocate the obligation differently.

This Section is a condition of the permission granted by this license. It does
not by itself claim governmental taxing power outside whatever lawful Garden
governance or contractual structure actually applies.

4. No outside-Garden use

No permission is granted under this license for operational, commercial,
production, deployment, or other exploitation of Covered Garden Material
outside a Garden implementation satisfying Sections 2 and 3.

Payment of the Garden contribution/tax does not convert an outside-Garden use
into a permitted use.

5. Unauthorized outside-Garden use and agreed economic remedy

By exercising any permission under this license, or otherwise assenting to these
terms while accessing, copying, implementing, modifying, distributing, or using
Covered Garden Material, a person or entity agrees that any outside-Garden use
of Covered Garden Material or legally protected Garden rights without applicable
approval is unauthorized.

For such unauthorized outside-Garden use, and to the maximum extent permitted by
applicable law, the user agrees to pay an amount equal to 1000% (ten times) of
all savings, gains, revenues, cost reductions, profits, economic advantages, or
other measurable benefits derived from or attributable to the unauthorized use
of Covered Garden Material or protected Garden rights. The calculation should
include direct and indirect benefits that can be established with reasonable
evidence and should avoid double counting the same economic benefit.

This 1000% amount is intended as an agreed contractual remedy for unauthorized
use where such a remedy is legally enforceable; it does not create intellectual-
property rights in unprotectable abstract ideas, facts, methods, or concepts. If
a court or other competent authority determines that the 1000% measure is
unenforceable, excessive, or constitutes an impermissible penalty, the amount
shall be reduced to the maximum lawful enforceable amount, without waiving any
other remedy available under contract, copyright, patent, trade-secret, unjust-
enrichment, restitution, or other applicable law.

Nothing in this Section grants permission for outside-Garden use merely because
a user is willing to pay the stated amount. Outside-Garden use remains
unlicensed unless separately approved by an authorized Garden licensing process.

6. Inspection, criticism, and evaluation

This license does not restrict rights that already exist independently under
applicable law. Public reading, citation, criticism, comparison, research, and
evaluation of the published material remain permitted to the extent allowed by
law and the repository's notices, provided those activities do not themselves
amount to an otherwise unlicensed practice or exploitation of protected Garden
rights.

7. No authority grant

This license grants no political, constitutional, governance, enforcement,
deployment, certification, or real-world authority. Intellectual-property
permission and Garden governance authority are separate.

8. Attribution and notices

Redistributions or permitted Garden implementations must preserve this LICENSE
and applicable copyright, patent, provenance, and use notices supplied with the
Covered Garden Material.

9. Termination

Permission under this license terminates automatically for a use that ceases to
satisfy Sections 2 or 3, or that becomes an outside-Garden use prohibited by
Section 4. Termination does not erase obligations or liabilities that arose
before termination.

10. No warranty

THE COVERED GARDEN MATERIAL IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, SAFETY, CORRECTNESS, CERTIFICATION, OR
FITNESS FOR DEPLOYMENT.

11. Legal boundary

Patentability, copyright scope, enforceability, independent creation, lawful
exceptions, exhaustion, compulsory licensing, interoperability rights, fair
use/fair dealing, and other legal questions depend on applicable law and actual
rights. This license must not be read as creating exclusive rights in abstract
ideas or facts where the law does not provide such rights.
